  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. I haven't run the tests or added a new one.\n\nFor an open bound, the clamped value was moved the wrong way. It computed `bound - dir`, but `dir` is `1` when clamping up to a minimum and `-1` when clamping down to a maximum. So `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returned `-1`, which is still out of range. It now returns `bound + dir`, so that case gives `1`. An open maximum behaves the same way, e.g. `max=5, max_open=True` clamps to `4`.\n\nClosed bounds weren't affected, which is why the existing clamp tests in `tests/test_types.py` didn't catch this. They only cover closed bounds.",
